WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.612
To close Part 1, here's what the four
collection gates leave in the evidence file.

2
00:00:04.612 --> 00:00:07.219
Each one keeps the
provider's raw response,

3
00:00:07.219 --> 00:00:11.762
the normalized notices and a manifest
with every call and its permission.

4
00:00:11.762 --> 00:00:14.574
Azure adds the alert plan and its results.

5
00:00:14.574 --> 00:00:19.257
Together they support monitoring external
providers, receiving their advisories,

6
00:00:19.257 --> 00:00:23.605
continuous monitoring, configuration
change control for announced changes,

7
00:00:23.605 --> 00:00:26.013
and contingency planning for maintenance.

8
00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:30.497
Part 2 picks up from there: Google
Cloud's incidents and its maintenance gap,

9
00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:34.982
then routing every notice that needs
action to an owner as a task, the weekly

10
00:00:34.982 --> 00:00:38.454
digest, and the evidence chain
the security officer keeps,

11
00:00:38.454 --> 00:00:40.262
with the dangers and rollback.

12
00:00:40.262 --> 00:00:43.581
To build Part 1's code,
use the developer workbook,

13
00:00:43.581 --> 00:00:48.476
Building Provider Notices, chapters
one to four, each with a fixture lab.

14
00:00:48.476 --> 00:00:53.000
And a last reminder: this guide is a
draft, awaiting the owner's review.

15
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:53.830
Thank you.
